The `abletonosc/` and `pythonosc/` directories are unmodified upstream code.
`manager.py` is also unmodified upstream code, vendored alongside
`abletonosc/` because `copilot/manager.py`'s `CopilotManager` does
`from ..manager import Manager` and subclasses it; without `manager.py` the
Remote Script cannot construct its Manager instance inside Live. (The
brief's copy list omitted `manager.py`; this is the one deviation from it,
made because Tasks 2 and later require a working Remote Script, not just an
importable `abletonosc.handler` module.)

The upstream `client/` directory (a standalone CLI/test client) is not
vendored: nothing in `abletonosc/`, `manager.py`, or `__init__.py` imports
it, so it is not needed for the Remote Script to run inside Live.

Our additions live in `copilot/`. Do not edit vendored files in place; add a
handler in `copilot/` and register it from `copilot/manager.py` instead.

`__init__.py` is NOT verbatim upstream. `manager.py` must stay byte-identical
to upstream (see above), so it cannot be edited to add master/return-track
handlers. Instead, `copilot/manager.py` defines `CopilotManager(Manager)`,
which overrides `init_api()` to call `super().init_api()` and then append
`MasterHandler`, `ReturnHandler`, `MixerHandler`, `DeviceRangeHandler`, and
`ViewOverrideHandler` to `self.handlers` (see Task 2 and later). `__init__.py`
was changed only to import `CopilotManager` from `.copilot.manager` and
return it from `create_instance()` instead of the upstream `Manager`. The
`try/except ImportError` wrapper that lets pytest import this package is
unchanged.
